      "text": "One metric I always find interesting when looking at token launches is demand relative to the actual allocation.\n\nIt offers a useful indication of market interest before a token even enters open trading.\n\nThe latest figures are particularly interesting for @1winToken, which I wrote about a while ago:\n\n$61M in commitments against a $3.9M allocation.\n\nThat's 15.64x oversubscribed.\n\n$1WIN is oversold after a 43% pullback from its launch peak, with a $0.049 support level close by and steady trading of $4M+ a day. \n\nReclaiming $0.059 would be the first sign of a real bounce, though the top 10 wallets still hold 83% of the supply.\n\nToken: https://jup.ag/tokens/FjPKUGnF5zBpdEv18gT8FJCtxh3MKrFkoeYekgYr1win",
